IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `it-types`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, personal income tax — GOAL 1: RESIDENCE.
--
--   "Is this natural person a New Zealand resident on this day?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2007_97.txt — ss YD 1,
-- YD 1B.

§ `Goal 1 — residence`

-- YD 1B "(2) A person who visits New Zealand is a non-resident visitor if—
-- (a) they are a natural person; and (b) their visit is for 275 or fewer
-- days, counting the days of arrival and departure as a whole day each; and
-- (c) they are personally present in New Zealand for 275 or fewer days in
-- total in an 18-month period that includes the period of the visit; and (d)
-- immediately before the first day they are personally present, they were
-- not resident in New Zealand and were not a transitional resident; and (e)
-- they are not undertaking work that— (i) is for a New Zealand resident ...;
-- or (ii) is offering goods or services in New Zealand ...; or (iii) requires
-- the person to be physically present in New Zealand; and (f) they, or
-- their spouse ..., are not receiving an entitlement under the family scheme;
-- and (g) they are lawfully present in New Zealand under the Immigration Act
-- 2009; and (h) they are resident ... or liable to tax in a country or
-- territory outside New Zealand on the basis of citizenship" ((f)-(h) added
-- after the independent pass).
@ref s YD 1B(2)
GIVEN r IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a non-resident visitor` r IF
        r's `days of the visit` AT MOST 275
    AND r's `days present in the 18 months including the visit` AT MOST 275
    AND NOT r's `resident or a transitional resident immediately before the visit`
    AND NOT r's `working in New Zealand in a way YD 1B(2)(e) excludes`
    AND r's `neither they nor their partner receive a family scheme entitlement`
    AND r's `lawfully present under the Immigration Act 2009`
    AND r's `resident abroad or taxed abroad on citizenship`

-- YD 1 "(2) Despite anything else in this section, a natural person is a New
-- Zealand resident if they have a permanent place of abode in New Zealand
-- ... (3) A natural person is a New Zealand resident if they are personally
-- present in New Zealand for more than 183 days in total in a 12-month
-- period. (4) If subsection (3) applies, the natural person is treated as
-- resident from the first of the 183 days until the natural person is treated
-- under subsection (5) as ceasing to be a New Zealand resident. (5) A natural
-- person treated as a New Zealand resident only under subsection (3) stops
-- being a New Zealand resident if they are personally absent from New Zealand
-- for more than 325 days in total in a 12-month period. (6) The natural
-- person is treated as not resident from the first of the 325 days ... (7)
-- Despite subsection (5), a natural person who is personally absent ... in
-- the service ... of the New Zealand Government is treated as a New Zealand
-- resident during the absence. ... (9) Despite subsection (3), a
-- non-resident seasonal worker is treated ... as a non-resident. ... (11)
-- Despite subsection (3), if a person is a non-resident visitor, they are
-- treated as a non-resident for the period they are a non-resident visitor".
@ref s YD 1(2)-(11)
@export Whether a natural person is a New Zealand resident on a day under s YD 1 of the Income Tax Act 2007 (NZ): always with a permanent place of abode in New Zealand; otherwise from the first of more than 183 days present in a 12-month period (not for a recognised seasonal worker or a non-resident visitor under YD 1B), until the first of more than 325 days absent in a 12-month period (unless absent in New Zealand Government service). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Residence facts`  @desc The permanent place of abode, the most days present and absent in a 12-month period with the first of each, Government service, seasonal work, and the non-resident visitor facts
      d IS A DATE  @desc The day in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a New Zealand resident` r `on` d IF
        r's `has a permanent place of abode in New Zealand`
    OR  (    NOT r's `a non-resident seasonal worker`
         AND NOT `is a non-resident visitor` r
         AND r's `most days present in a 12-month period` GREATER THAN 183
         AND (CONSIDER r's `first of the days present`
              WHEN JUST first THEN first AT MOST d
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
         AND NOT (    r's `most days absent in a 12-month period` GREATER THAN 325
                  AND NOT r's `absent in the service of the New Zealand Government`
                  AND (CONSIDER r's `first of the days absent`
                       WHEN JUST first THEN first AT MOST d
                       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)))
